course: dictionary
lesson: 804
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A beggar is a person who is very poor and lives by asking people for money or food. In a story, you might see «a beggar at the palace gate», and you can picture someone with little or nothing. Read the words around beggar to find out which meaning the writer chose.
explain: Odysseus came home in disguise: «he came in dressed as a beggar», so the word describes how he looked and pretended to be. Here it is a person who looks needy, not a word for someone who is rude. The sentence around the word gives you the clue.
explain: In everyday talk, beggar can be friendly or cross. The Otter grumbles «Greedy beggars!» while the Rat brings food and drink, so the context shows it is a friendly tease. Words can have a kind or unkind feeling, so always check the clues before you decide.
fact: A beggar is a person who is very poor and asks others for money or food.
fact: Used as a word for a person, beggar can be kind or cross: «lucky beggar» and «you little beggar».
fact: «Greedy beggars!» is a friendly tease, not a real insult.
fact: «Beggars can't be choosers» means if you need help, you must accept what you get.
fact: As a formal verb, beggar means to make very poor, and «beggar belief» means be impossible to believe.
exercise: «The beggar sat by the palace gate, hungry and cold.» What is a beggar? | *A person who is very poor and asks others for money or food | A king who lives in a palace | A rich merchant | A kind of horse
exercise: The Otter grins and says «Greedy beggars!» as the Rat brings food. Is it a real insult? | Yes, it is a cruel insult | *No, it is a friendly tease | Yes, the Otter is very angry with the Rat | It means the Rat has no food
exercise: As a formal verb, what does beggar mean? | To be very rich | To give away gifts | *To make very poor | To ask for money politely
test: «Odysseus came in dressed as a beggar.» What does beggar describe here? | A bird in the hall | A prince who is hiding | *A person who looks poor and needy | A wizard with a magic staff
test: «Beggars can't be choosers» means what? | Poor people should be allowed to pick the best food | *If you need help, you must accept what you get | Beggars never say no to anything | You can only beg in the morning
exam: «Beggar belief» means what? | To feel very sorry for someone | *To be impossible to believe | To beg for a belief in fairy tales | To ask a stranger for money
